  "description": "<div>\n  <p>The roads between cities form an undirected tree, but each road currently permits travel in only the listed direction <code>[from,to]</code>. Reverse as few roads as possible so every city can travel along directed roads to city <code>0</code>.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 6, connections = [[0,1],[1,3],[2,3],[4,0],[4,5]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3</pre>\n  <p>The roads 0→1, 1→3 and 4→5 point away from zero.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 3, connections = [[1,0],[2,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>Both roads already point to city zero.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1, connections = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>One city needs no roads.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 100</code>; city labels are <code>0..n-1</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>connections.length = n-1</code> and the underlying undirected roads form a tree.</li>\n    <li>Each listed road connects two different cities.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
